issue.body:
Next code started working differently after update to Mockito 2.x.

```
@RunWith(MockitoJUnitRunner.Silent.class)
public class ChangePinActivityPresenterShould
{
  @InjectMocks private ChangePinActivityPresenter presenter;

  @Test
  public void delay_view_finish_until_subscribed()
    throws Exception
  {
    presenter.finishFlow();

    presenter.subscribe(viewMock);

    verify(viewMock).finish();
  }
}

class ChangePinActivityPresenter
  implements ChangePinActivityContract.Presenter
{
  private final Analytics analytics;
  private final PendingActionsProcessor<ChangePinActivityContract.View> pendingActionsProcessor;

  @Nullable private ChangePinActivityContract.View view;
  @Nullable private Action1<ChangePinActivityContract.View> finishAction;

  ChangePinActivityPresenter(
    @NonNull Analytics analytics,
    @NonNull PendingActionsProcessor<ChangePinActivityContract.View> pendingActionsProcessor
  )
  {
    this.analytics = analytics;
    this.pendingActionsProcessor = pendingActionsProcessor;
  }

  @Override
  public void finishFlow()
  {
    if (view != null)
    {
      view.finish();
    }
    else
    {
      finishAction = ChangePinActivityContract.View::finish;
    }
  }

  @Override
  public void subscribe(@NonNull ChangePinActivityContract.View view)
  {
    this.view = view;

    if (finishAction != null)
    {
      finishAction.call(view);
    }
    else
    {
      pendingActionsProcessor.applyAllPendingChanges(view);
    }
  }
}
```

What I observing that **Mockito** uses non-default constructor (or maybe field injection) and field injection (or just it). The test above expects that after test setup `view` field is null. I read [javadoc](http://site.mockito.org/mockito/docs/current/org/mockito/InjectMocks.html) but looks like I have a combination of final/non-final fields and this case is not explained clearly.

I use Java8 on Mack Sierra and my Mockito version is 2.2.0.

